{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>His son that was born to him, etc.</b> Meaning: since he already had another son, namely Yishma'el, therefore it says ״that was born to him״ — referring to a matter fitting for him to be called by, for the purpose of his desire, which Scripture did not say at the birth of Yishma'el. And it says <b>whom Sarah bore to him</b>, alluding to what they would always pray for: Avraham would say, ״Let all my seed be from this righteous one,״ and Sarah likewise, etc. Corresponding to her prayer it says ״bore to him,״ and corresponding to his prayer it says ״Sarah.״" "<b>Further,</b> it intends to give a reason for the naming of his name Yitzchak, because the old woman bore to the old man, and thus it says (Genesis 21:6): ״צְחֹק עָשָׂה לִי״, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:37.151939834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}